  "summary_text": "Kyle, Port Washington is running strong operationally but hitting a real performance headwind in October \u2014 you're down 8% MTD, and even after adjusting for calendar mix, you're still 10.4% below expectation. The gap isn't capacity; yesterday you ran 5 groomers at $540/groomer-day, well above your trailing-30-day baseline of $471, so the team is executing. The problem is front-of-house: retail cratered 36% yesterday and is down significantly MTD, and add-on attachment fell from 62% to 54%. This is a discipline issue, not a staffing issue \u2014 your bathers are up 7 hours versus average, core grooms are solid, but upselling and retail focus have slipped. Hicksville is the opposite story and worth celebrating: you're up 62% yesterday, 74% week-to-date, and 13% MTD while running at DOW-adjusted +4.7% \u2014 real outperformance. That location is finding its rhythm. Glen Cove is opening cleanly but tomorrow and the next seven days are zeroed out on groomer scheduling; confirm if that's intentional or a data error.\n\nAcross both primary locations, you're sitting on $458k in lapse pool annual value \u2014 160 drifting, 168 lapsed, 188 dormant. Port Washington alone has $318k. That's a reactivation play, not a loss.\n\nPort Washington: reorder Shanti's Medical Journey, X-Small Treat Table, and Jack&Pup Braided Bully immediately (all at zero). Whitening toothpaste is at reorder threshold. Hicksville: Cannoli and X-Small Treat Table are running negative inventory; prioritize those and small pink paper bags.\n\n**Capacity & coverage: Port Washington has 7 groomer-days scheduled today and tomorrow with 30 combined bather hours across both days; next 7 days 36 groomer-days, 83 bather hours. Hicksville: 4 today, 5 tomorrow, 22 groomer-days next 7 days, zero bather hours scheduled. Glen Cove: zero groomers scheduled today through next 7 days \u2014 confirm intent.**"
